## Prerequisites

- CMake 3.15 or higher
- A C++{{ cpp_standard | regex_replace(pat="C\\+\\+", repl="") }} compatible compiler
- [Conan {{ conan_version }}](https://conan.io/) package manager

## Setup

### Install Conan

For Conan 2.x (recommended):
```bash
pip install "conan>=2.0"
```

For Conan 1.x:
```bash
pip install "conan<2.0"
```

## Building

### 1. Install Dependencies

Install Conan dependencies:
```bash
conan install . --build=missing -s:h build_type={{ build_type }}
```

### 2. Configure CMake

Configure the project with Conan toolchain:
```bash
cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE={{ build_type }} -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=conan_toolchain.cmake
```

### 3. Build

Build the project:
```bash
cmake --build build --config {{ build_type }}
```

### 4. Run

{% if project_type == "executable" %}Run the executable:
```bash
./build/{{ project_name | snake_case }}
```{% else %}Use the library:
The library will be built in `build/lib/` and can be linked against other projects.{% endif %}

## Testing

{% if include_tests %}
This project uses [Catch2](https://github.com/catchorg/Catch2) for testing, managed via Conan.

### Running Tests

Build and run tests:
```bash
cmake --build build --target test
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

Or run the test executable directly:
```bash
./build/tests
```
{% else %}
Testing is not enabled for this project. To enable testing, regenerate the project with `include_tests=true`.
{% endif %}

## Adding Dependencies

To add new Conan dependencies:

1. Edit `conanfile.txt` and add your requirements to the `[requires]` section
2. Reinstall dependencies: `conan install . --build=missing`
3. Update `CMakeLists.txt` to use the new packages

Example:
```txt
[requires]
fmt/9.1.0
spdlog/1.11.0
catch2/3.4.0
```

